WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:17,980
Why did you expect that my alpha fetal protein to a marker test will take a while to drop

00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:18,980
after surgery?

00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:23,640
Well, I didn't, if I said that I didn't, I misspoke, I didn't expect it to, it just

00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:29,240
that's, I've just seen that sometimes it could take, you know, a few weeks for your

00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:31,340
to a marker to drop post surgery.

00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:39,500
Now, I did a brief, you know, search on the literature on any data of this, and I just

00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:47,740
can't find any studies on when the tumor markers will drop and post surgery.

00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:53,340
So that in fact, there's very little on the AFP tumor marker with breast cancer.

00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:58,500
It's literally almost most of the research is done on liver cancer.

00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:06,300
So it's hard to find any research on this stuff, so it's, it's very difficult.

00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:12,300
It's just through the years of trying to help people with this, my, what I've noticed

00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:19,940
is that two markers don't necessarily drop suddenly post surgery, so that's what I meant

00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:20,940
to say.

00:01:20,940 --> 00:01:23,700
Why might other two markers rise after surgery?

00:01:24,020 --> 00:01:28,820
Again, you know, you remember that, you know, two markers are just one test, and it's

00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:30,300
not perfect.

00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:37,340
The only data that you can really find of what causes two markers to rise is, is, is, use

00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:38,340
of chemotherapy.

00:01:38,340 --> 00:01:42,380
And that certainly doesn't happen every time, you know, we have patients probably on this

00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:47,140
call that did chemotherapy, that didn't cause their two markers to spike.

00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:51,380
But I'll get, you know, tell you for sure, over the years, I've seen that lots of times where

00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:56,460
people would start chemotherapy, so the two markers literally just won't skyrocket.

00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:59,500
Some people's body doesn't respond the same way.

00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:06,220
So all I'm saying is that there's not really any data that says that it's a bad thing that

00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:08,220
two markers are dropping quickly.

00:02:08,220 --> 00:02:13,100
There's no data that went to a marker's will drop and, and how much they will drop after

00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:14,100
surgery.

00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:17,340
It's just, it's a speculation at this point.

